# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=escort (The Long Haul),
# spec=mage:frost, style=auto, view=844x390,touch, save=carried (behaves as
# fresh per #273 -- playbot's own port is per-run, so localStorage's origin
# never actually carries between invocations).
#
# New: every prior style=auto battleground reading on direction.md's #7 was
# either a healer (druid:restoration, flags, genuine touch) or a tank
# (paladin:protection, escort, genuine touch), plus one damage spec that
# only ever fell back to `good` because its viewport had no touch toggle
# (druid:balance, flags, 1280x800 desktop). Nobody has run a ranged damage
# spec under auto on a real touch viewport, on any map -- this is that
# reading, and it lands on escort specifically, the one map where auto has
# already shown a passive tank survive untouched while its team lost ground.
# A mage's own kit needs nothing but a target in range (no ally-health
# precondition a heal has, no self-only defensive a tank's taunt needs to
# land on someone else) -- so if auto's missing steering ever lets a
# stationary body connect anything at all on this map, a ranged nuker
# sitting at its own spawn point is the best-case kit to show it.
open
tap battleground
tap map:escort
targets
tap class:mage:frost
shot class-picked
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot bg-start
state
ui
play auto 90
shot mid1
state
bill
wait 3
play auto 90
shot mid2
state
bill
wait 3
play auto 90
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
